      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T16:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this takes a `begin**` and `end*` like this, then there is no need to (rather confusingly) also return an `SkUnichar`. Instead, this should just move `*begin` to the end of the current emoji sequence (which means not moving it at all if there is no emoji sequence) and then the caller can hold onto the \"old begin\" pointer and compare it to `*begin` after this call and see if they are different.\n\nAlternatively, this could just return a `bool` for if an emoji sequence was found (implicitly meaning that `*begin` has changed).\n\nEither way the caller would know the range based on the old value of `*begin` and the new value after calling this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 122,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "b42cae3bc355473deb4fc44332c5607f44892980",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
